I tried to refute all five findings by reading the cited lines and running grep. All five survive. The evidence for the first four is exactly as described. The fifth (capit_lever_selfcheck) is accurate as quoted, but whether it is a bug or a deliberate pin is a judgement call.

<<<VERIFY_JSON>>>
{"verified": [
{"file": "/home/trido/thanhdt/WorkingClaude/append_cctg_rate.py", "line": 161, "survives": true, "note": "Confirmed. L150 skips the SKIP check when --force is set. cctg_events_df() (cctg_rate_vn.py L62-87) loads every CSV row with nothing filtered out, so if args.effective is already a row then eff <= max(time) and L161 [REDACTED] exits. The removal at L239-240 cannot be reached for an existing date, even though help text L101 says it can ('append even if effective_date exists')."},
{"file": "/home/trido/thanhdt/WorkingClaude/append_deposit_rate.py", "line": 317, "survives": true, "note": "Confirmed. L317 is `real_today = date.today().isoformat()` and the file has no _ICT/ZoneInfo. It drives L324 (eff_age_days), L344 (collected != real_today) and L390-401 (source age). The sibling append_cctg_rate.py L117 uses datetime.now(_ICT)."},
{"file": "/home/trido/thanhdt/WorkingClaude/bank_compounder_screen.py", "line": 132, "survives": true, "note": "Confirmed. L132 builds rs from picks_map.keys(), which comes only from sel.groupby('d') (L110-113), so a month with 0 qualifiers is merged into a multi-month period while metrics() L161 still uses yrs=len(r)/12. cnt is built only from qualifying months, so 'months 0' (L183) and months_zero (L286) are [REDACTED] 0. Docstring L32 says '7-8 liquid names 2013-17'. aviation_screen.simulate does have hold_cash_when_empty (L73/88)."},
{"file": "/home/trido/thanhdt/WorkingClaude/compounder_screen.py", "line": 104, "survives": true, "note": "Confirmed. L104 is rebal_sorted = sorted(picks.keys()), with picks/cnt built only from sel.groupby('d') (L80-85). exit_ = next_session(d_next) spans the empty months, and metrics uses yrs=len(r)/12. Periods with no prices are also dropped (`if not rets: continue`)."},
{"file": "/home/trido/thanhdt/WorkingClaude/capit_lever_selfcheck.py", "line": 340, "survives": true, "note": "Evidence accurate: A7 (L339-340) and G1 (L1394-1397) assert that the real config has enabled is True. The guideline exists: coding_guidelines_ext §23, 'Hệ luận' item 2 says to assert on an invariant, not a value (seen in the mike/agents/Taylor worktree copy, since kb/ is not in the WorkingClaude root). Caveat: the comment at L335-338 shows the pin is a deliberate snapshot of the user's [REDACTED]22 decision, so this is a design-policy finding, not a logic bug. A6/G2/G3 pin values the same way."}
]}
<<<END_VERIFY>>>
